{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning, I've the obs done. Blood pressure is one oh nine over seventy-seven, pulse seventy-two, weight today seventy-one kilos. Last time in March you were sixty-eight.",
  "[SEG0002] person_1 (NURSE): Ah sorry, I misread the pulse. It's seventy-six, not seventy-two.",
  "[SEG0003] person_2 (DOCTOR): Grand. Umm, the screen is after freezing on me. What has you in?",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (PATIENT): Sweats.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sweats. Say that again?",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (PATIENT): Mornings.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Shaky with them?",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (NURSE): He skips the breakfast. The sweats and the shakes come on before he eats anything.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (NURSE): The daughter rang the surgery. Said he was confused the one morning, just the once, and he came back to himself after a cup of tea.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Confused? Sorry, say that again, I was on the wrong tab.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (NURSE): Confused, the once. It cleared.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (PATIENT): Once.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): How long are the morning sweats going?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): Weeks.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hold on, this yoke is crawling. Err, did ye get caught in that rain? Desperate out there.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (NURSE): The grandkids were down for the hurling in the park and they called the whole thing off. Pitch was a lake. Youngest had the jersey on already, he was raging the whole way home.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ah sure. I was stuck on the M50 nearly an hour, nothing moving past the Red Cow. They say the same again tomorrow.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right, where was I. The tablets. You're on the gliclazide?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (NURSE): Gliklazide eighty milligrams, one every morning. Metforman five hundred milligrams twice a day. Both for the sugar. On them years.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): The metformin, again? I only caught half of that.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (NURSE): Five hundred milligrams, twice a day.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain with the sweats?",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): And the heart racing at all?",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): This is most likely the sugar dropping in the mornings, the gliclazide on an empty stomach. That's my working read of it.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): The nurse takes bloods Thursday morning. Fasting from midnight, and don't take the morning gliclazide till after the bloods and you've had the breakfast. We'll do a fasting glucose and the hba1c.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (NURSE): I'll book him in Thursday morning so.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): If those are borderline we do the third test, a longer sugar profile. Not booking that now. And if the confusion comes back we'll arrange a scan of the head.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll see you in two weeks with the results. Eat the breakfast every morning, don't be skipping it, and take the gliclazide with the food."
 ],
